// The source the HTML data app (public/index.html) queries.
//
// The page could interpolate a `where:` into every query string instead, and an
// earlier version did. Givens are better for the same reason they are better on
// a dashboard: the value is bound by the server as a typed parameter rather than
// pasted into query text, and the page ends up filtering by *the same* five
// givens the dashboards and the notebook filter by. That is what lets a drill
// click seed a value the dashboards would also accept, so a link out of the data
// app and a link out of a dashboard mean the same thing.
//
// It exists as its own file because Malloy's given namespace is per-file: a
// query can only reference a given the file it runs against imports. The
// notebook does the same thing in its first cell (`orders_in_scope`), and
// dashboards/_shared.malloy does it for the composite dashboard's tiles. This is
// the data app's copy of that idea, with all five givens rather than a subset,
// because the page renders one control row that every tab shares.
//
// No `# artifact` tag, so this is not a dashboard: just a model the page reads.
##! experimental.givens
import "storefront.malloy"
import { CATEGORY, BRAND, REGION, SINCE, MIN_SALE } from "givens.malloy"

#(doc) Order lines narrowed by the data app's control row. Every tile queries this.
source: scoped_orders is order_items extend {
  where:
    category ~ $CATEGORY
    and brand ~ $BRAND
    and region ~ $REGION
    and created_at >= $SINCE
    and sale_price ~ $MIN_SALE
}
